# StreamTube — Video Upload Handshake (SI-03.7)
# =============================================================================
# VS Code "REST Client" (humao.rest-client) file. Run requests top-to-bottom.
# Every scenario below was executed live against localhost and returns the
# documented status. Requests are chained: tokens, publicId and the part ETag
# flow automatically from earlier named responses — the ONLY manual step is
# pasting the email-confirmation token (see step 2/2b).
#
# Prereqs (host):
#   cd nestjs-project && docker compose up -d
#   curl http://localhost:3000            # -> 200
#   Mailpit UI: http://localhost:8025     # confirmation emails land here
#
# Re-running from scratch: bump @ownerEmail / @strangerEmail (a used email
# returns 409 on register).
# =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@mailpit = http://localhost:8025
@ownerEmail = owner1@streamtube.local
@strangerEmail = stranger1@streamtube.local
@password = password123

# Paste the `token=...` value from the confirmation email here (step 2 / 2b).
@ownerConfirmToken = 36ba3a10304735f77cc7c563b04956177091ea0b5bfe1ed76d6636456f12562d
@strangerConfirmToken = 58ebd2a3994fada010b45da683d437b042b71474af1936db30fafd574e76cc0d


# ── OWNER: register → confirm → login ────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Register the owner  (-> 201). Sends a confirmation email to Mailpit.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{ownerEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Read the owner's confirmation email, then copy its `token=...` into
###    @ownerConfirmToken above. (Or just open the Mailpit UI: http://localhost:8025)
GET {{mailpit}}/api/v1/search?query=to:{{ownerEmail}}&limit=1

### 3. Confirm the owner's email  (-> 204)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/confirm-email?token={{ownerConfirmToken}}

### 4. Login as owner  (-> 200, captures access_token)
# @name loginOwner
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{ownerEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}" }


# ── STRANGER: register → confirm → login (for the 403 non-owner scenario) ─────

### 5. Register the stranger  (-> 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{strangerEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2b. Read the stranger's confirmation email; copy `token=...` into
###     @strangerConfirmToken above.
GET {{mailpit}}/api/v1/search?query=to:{{strangerEmail}}&limit=1

### 6. Confirm the stranger's email  (-> 204)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/confirm-email?token={{strangerConfirmToken}}

### 7. Login as stranger  (-> 200, captures access_token)
# @name loginStranger
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{strangerEmail}}", "password": "{{password}}" }


# ── HAPPY PATH: draft → part-urls → PUT part → complete ──────────────────────

### A. Create draft  (-> 201). Captures publicId + uploadId.
# @name createDraft
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filename": "demo.mp4",
  "contentType": "video/mp4",
  "sizeBytes": 52428800,
  "title": "Flow demo"
}

### B. Issue presigned part URLs  (-> 200). URLs target the public gateway
###    (localhost:9000), never minio:9000.
# @name partUrls
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{createDraft.response.body.publicId}}/upload/part-urls
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "partNumbers": [1] }

### C. PUT the part bytes directly to the presigned gateway URL  (-> 200).
###    The response ETag is reused verbatim in the next request.
# @name putPart
PUT {{partUrls.response.body.parts[0].url}}
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

streamtube-live-payload

### D. Complete the upload  (-> 200 processing). The ETag from step C carries
###    its own quotes, which become the JSON string delimiters here.
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{createDraft.response.body.publicId}}/upload/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parts": [ { "partNumber": 1, "eTag": {{putPart.response.headers.ETag}} } ] }


# ── OWNERSHIP + ABORT (uses a second, fresh draft) ───────────────────────────

### E. Create a second draft to exercise 403 + abort  (-> 201)
# @name createDraft2
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "filename": "d2.mp4", "contentType": "video/mp4", "sizeBytes": 1048576 }

### F. Complete by the NON-OWNER stranger  (-> 403 FORBIDDEN_NOT_OWNER).
###    The ownership guard rejects before any state/parts check.
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{createDraft2.response.body.publicId}}/upload/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{loginStranger.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parts": [ { "partNumber": 1, "eTag": "\"x\"" } ] }

### G. Abort the upload as owner  (-> 204 No Content). Idempotent.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{createDraft2.response.body.publicId}}/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.access_token}}


# ── ERROR SCENARIOS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### H. sizeBytes over the 10 GB ceiling  (-> 400 FILE_TOO_LARGE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "filename": "huge.mp4", "contentType": "video/mp4", "sizeBytes": 10737418241 }

### I. Non-video contentType  (-> 415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "filename": "doc.pdf", "contentType": "application/pdf", "sizeBytes": 1024 }

### J. Missing access token  (-> 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "filename": "x.mp4", "contentType": "video/mp4", "sizeBytes": 1024 }

### K. Unknown publicId  (-> 404 VIDEO_NOT_FOUND)
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos/doesNotExist/upload/part-urls
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "partNumbers": [1] }
